# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# 301s from the URL a guide used to live at. A guide moves category when the
# category it belonged to did not exist yet — /visas/ was planned from the
# start and opened late, so four guides spent their first days filed under the
# nearest thing available. Google had already seen them there.
#
# These are permanent on purpose. A 301 passes what the old URL earned and
# tells the index to replace the entry rather than keep both; a 302 keeps the
# old URL in the index and splits the signal between two addresses for the
# same page.
#
# Nothing here expires. An old URL with one inbound link somewhere on the
# internet is worth more than a tidy file.

